---
import ToolLayout from '../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import Checker from '../../../components/Checker.astro';
import { pipChecker } from '../../../lib/checker/pip';
---
<ToolLayout
  title="PIP points self-check"
  eyebrow="Free self-check"
  description="Free PIP points calculator. Go through all 12 PIP activities in plain English and see how many points may apply to you. Private: answers stay on your device."
  lead="Go through the 12 PIP activities one at a time and see roughly how many points may apply to you, and how much PIP that could mean."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Benefits', href: '/benefits/' },
    { name: 'PIP', href: '/benefits/pip/' },
    { name: 'Points self-check', href: '/benefits/pip/points-checker/' },
  ]}
>
  <Checker def={pipChecker} showPoints>
    <p>This check takes about 10 minutes. There are 3 quick questions about you, then one question for each PIP activity.</p>
    <h3>Two rules to keep in mind</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Think about most days.</strong> If your condition changes from day to day, pick the answer that is true on more than half of days.</li>
      <li><strong>Think about doing it reliably.</strong> Only say you can do something if you can do it safely, well enough, again and again, and in a reasonable time. Pain, tiredness and the effect on you afterwards all count.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>At the end you can print or save your answers as a PDF to help you fill in the PIP form.</p>
  </Checker>
  <section class="prose" slot="after" style="padding-bottom:var(--space-3xl)">
    <h2>How PIP points work</h2>
    <p>PIP has two parts. The <strong>daily living</strong> part looks at 10 activities, and the <strong>mobility</strong> part looks at 2. Each activity has a list of statements worth between 0 and 12 points. Only the highest statement that applies in each activity counts.</p>
    <p>You need <strong>8 points</strong> in a part to get the standard rate, and <strong>12 points</strong> to get the enhanced rate. You can get one part, both parts, or neither.</p>
    <p>Read <a href="/benefits/pip/activities/">the 12 activities explained</a> for more detail and examples.</p>
  </section>
</ToolLayout>

<script>
  import { initChecker } from '../../../lib/checker/engine';
  import { scorePip } from '../../../lib/checker/pip';
  initChecker('pip', scorePip);
</script>
